# Byte-stable checkouts -- git stores and restores files exactly as committed.
#
# Reason: `core.autocrlf=true` is set system-wide on this machine. Without this
# rule git rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so a fresh clone would carry CR bytes
# that this workspace forbids, `checksum_check.py` and the encoding conditions in
# `provenance_check.py` would fail on a clone while passing locally, and the
# SHA-256 values in CHECKSUM.sha256 would no longer describe the checked-out tree.
#
# "* -text" disables EOL conversion on both add and checkout. It does not modify
# any file content; it only stops git from doing so. The sub-repository carries
# the same rule in guinand-weil-rigorous-numerics-main/.gitattributes for the
# same reason, stated there against PROVENANCE.txt and its own manifest.
* -text
